    "subject": "Chemical Reaction and Engineering",
    "chapter": "Conversion, Yield, and Selectivity",
    "topic": "Conversion",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<ul>\r\n<li>Conversion (X) measures the extent to which a reactant is transformed into products during a chemical reaction.</li>\r\n<li>It is calculated as the ratio of the change in the moles of reactant to the initial moles of reactant.</li>\r\n<li>X = (Initial moles of reactant - Moles of reactant at any time) / Initial moles of reactant.</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "",
