    "discipline": "Chemical",
    "subject": "Chemical Reaction and Engineering",
    "chapter": "Conversion, Yield, and Selectivity",
    "topic": "Selectivity",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<ul>\r\n<li>Selectivity is the ratio of the yield of a specific product to the total yield of all products in a reaction.</li>\r\n<li>It measures how efficient a reaction is in producing the desired product.</li>\r\n<li>Selectivity (%) = (Yield of desired product / Total yield of all products) x 100%.</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "important": "",
