    "subject": "Chemical Reaction and Engineering",
    "chapter": "Reactor Types",
    "topic": "Gas Phase",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Gas phase reactors are vessels or systems in which chemical reactions take place in the gaseous phase. These reactors are essential in industries for producing chemicals, energy, and materials.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Types of Gas Phase Reactions: Gas phase reactions can be classified into homogeneous (single-phase) and heterogeneous (multi-phase) reactions. Homogeneous reactions involve reactants and products in the gas phase, while heterogeneous reactions may involve gas-solid, gas-liquid, or gas-solid-liquid interactions.</p>",
