    "topic": "Eddy Diffusion",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p>Eddy diffusion, a fundamental concept in fluid dynamics, refers to the random and chaotic mixing of fluid particles within a flowing fluid. It occurs due to the presence of turbulent flow, characterized by eddies or vortices of various sizes and velocities.</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Eddy_diffusion-cropped.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eddy_diffusion-cropped.svg\">Fquaren</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
