    "discipline": "Chemical",
    "subject": "Mass Transfer and Separation",
    "chapter": "Molecular Diffusion",
    "topic": "Steady and Unsteady State",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Molecular diffusion is the spontaneous movement of particles (molecules or ions) from an area of high concentration to an area of low concentration.</p>\r\n\r\nFick's First Law:<br/>\r\nDescribes steady-state molecular diffusion.\r\nMathematical Representation: \r\n\\[J=−D \\dfrac{dC}{dx}\\]\r\n​\t\r\nJ is the molar flux.<br/>\r\nD is the diffusion coefficient (diffusivity).<br/>\r\n$\\dfrac{dC}{dx}$ is the concentration gradient.",
