    "discipline": "Chemical",
    "subject": "Process Control",
    "chapter": "Control Loop Design and Hardware",
    "topic": "Conceptual Process Control",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Process control involves managing and manipulating variables in a system to ensure it operates in a desired manner. In chemical engineering, this includes maintaining specified conditions and optimizing process performance. A control system typically consists of sensors (to measure process variables), controllers (to implement control strategies), actuators (to adjust process conditions), and process models (mathematical representations of the system).</p>",
