    "topic": "Fugacity",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Fugacity is the measure of the tendency of a gas to escape or expand.</p>\r\n<p>The ratio of Fugacity (f) to the pressure (P) is known as Fugacity Coefficient. It is dimensionless and depends upon the nature of the gas, temperature and pressure.</p>\r\n\\[\\phi = \\dfrac{f}{P}\\]\r\n<p>For an ideal gas, fugacity and pressure are equal, so $\\phi$ = 1</p>",
